# 14 October 2026: the vector module on a SCENE of any reference. One shot is chosen from the bible (a graphic or a text card
# first), one frame is grabbed, the part of it that looks most like UI (sharp edges, few colours) is traced by the F2 vectoriser,
# and every traced layer is sorted so the two modules are never confused:
#   VECTOR   editable shapes, text outlines, icons, UI components (rect, rounded_rect, circle, line, path ...) -> asset.svg and
#            component.html (the palette as CSS variables)
#   SHADER   blur, glow, gradient fields (backgrounds with a linear or radial paint, any layer with an optical blur) -> the shader
#            bank (shader_hint of each layer says which blocks)
#   RESIDUAL photograph, texture, anything no primitive or path explains -> a plate, not a vector
# Reference pixels (the frame, the crop, the side-by-side picture) stay in the reference cache; the workshop keeps only the
# private 1:1 assets (params.json, svg, html, numbers). FR : le module vecteur sur une scene de n'importe quelle video.
